package m22history001run
    provides [checks, expected_vector, observe, case_body, descriptor, context, check, check_ref, expected_check, evidence, observation, failed, test_case]
    uses [text]

/// M22 HISTORY-001 "SQL queries: build/emitted/negative run shape".
/// Source: tests/integration/sql_test.go symbol TestCurrentSQLQueries
/// (L46-177); build helper buildAt (L89-103); identity legs
/// (L104-116); emitted state/unit needles (L117-146); optional
/// strict TypeScript leg (L147-152); negative manifests (L153-176).
/// Disposition: migrate (this row ports TestCurrentSQLQueries to
/// ordinary Can functions; the old Go harness stays until the
/// integrator retires it after every linked row, variant, environment
/// and control has accepted evidence).
/// Protects (this file): the build/emit/negative shape: the build
/// command with buildID/directory keys, repeated and relocated build
/// identity, the program/state.ts path plus its eight emitted wiring
/// needles, the single packages/*/*.ts program unit with its open
/// and close calls, the optional CAN_TSC strict leg, and the four
/// negative manifests with their rejection needles.
/// ADAPTATION (recorded, with source lines): rebuild-same and
/// relocated-same pin the L106/L114 equality predicates as bool
/// expectations; emit needles pin the exact L121-126/L140-142 source
/// spellings; tsc pins record the optional leg (CAN_TSC unset skips)
/// without claiming a live run (accept_after P23 unmet); negative
/// needles pin the L158-161 want strings.
/// Facet map (sql_test.go legs): build-cmd pins build (L91);
/// build-id-key and build-dir-key pin buildID/directory (L96-97);
/// rebuild-same pins the rebuild predicate (L106-108);
/// relocated-same pins the relocated predicate (L114-116); state-path
/// pins program/state.ts (L117); emit-pools, emit-optional,
/// emit-query-one, emit-query-optional, emit-query-rows,
/// emit-execute, emit-id-shape and emit-note-shape pin the state
/// needles (L121-126); program-glob pins packages/*/*.ts (L132);
/// program-count pins one unit (L133); unit-open and unit-close pin
/// the unit calls (L140-142); tsc-gate pins CAN_TSC (L147);
/// tsc-strict pins --strict (L148); neg-count pins four negatives
/// (L153); neg-cardinality, neg-param-type, neg-row-type and
/// neg-undeclared pin the rejection needles (L158-161).
/// Report/descriptor semantics live in
/// history-001-queries-semantics.can; the roots-green pin lives in
/// history-001-roots-green.can.
/// Variants: negative manifest cardinality, parameter type, row type,
/// undeclared (the L153 table, in order); each carries its rejection
/// needle.
/// Environment: CAN_BUN_ARCHIVE gate; requires can-bun-archive;
/// CAN_TSC optional.
/// Logical gates SUITE/CAN/BUILD/DIAG/WORK and C/R/N/S/A identities
/// bind at P23; no live run now. The offline legs additionally use
/// /usr/bin/sandbox-exec plus the bundled runtime/bun (recorded
/// mechanism, not waived). Descriptor timeout 240000ms mirrors the Go
/// 4-minute ctx (L51).
/// Delegated oracles: none.
/// Execution credit: NOT claimed (accept_after P23 unmet).
/// Case history/queries-run checks: build-cmd, build-id-key,
/// build-dir-key, rebuild-same, relocated-same, state-path,
/// emit-pools, emit-optional, emit-query-one, emit-query-optional,
/// emit-query-rows, emit-execute, emit-id-shape, emit-note-shape,
/// program-glob, program-count, unit-open, unit-close, tsc-gate,
/// tsc-strict, neg-count, neg-cardinality, neg-param-type,
/// neg-row-type, neg-undeclared.
/// Shared old files untouched; retirement is a later integrator decision.

